systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.j2wsK6IsW5yMW1jW","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"p6IUSSIZdi3WWF2G","name":"Limited Incorporeality","type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":200000,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A hieroglyph scorpion's unusual two-dimensional nature limits its incorporeality. The scorpion cannot pass through solid objects, though corporeal creatures can still pass through the hieroglyph scorpion.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"category":"defensive","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"4waU8GuJZP0qFiAg","name":"Reanimation","type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":300000,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>When a hieroglyph scorpion is destroyed, it re-forms, [[/br 2d4 #days]]{2d4 days} later within its mural, fully healed. A hieroglyph scorpion can be permanently destroyed only by destroying the mural which it was created to protect.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["arcane"],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"category":"defensive","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"H23fIYp3KKrWkqDg","name":"Inscription Venom","type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":400000,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> @Check[type:fortitude|dc:28|name:Inscription Venom DC|traits:arcane, incapacitation, transmutation|showDC:gm]{Fortitude};</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 6 rounds;</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 1</strong> @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.AJh5ex99aV6VTggg]{Off-Guard} (1 round);</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 2</strong> off-guard and @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{Slowed 1} (1 round);</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 3</strong> off-guard and @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{Slowed 2} (1 round);</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 4</strong> The victim is permanently petrified, and its physical body (including all its possessions) are magically inscribed onto the nearest flat surface, such as a wall or floor tile.</p>\n<p>No physical trace of the victim remains except its inscription. An inscribed creature can be recovered from the mural by targeting its inscription with @Compendium[pf2e.spells-srd.Pr1ruNTbzGn3H9w5]{Stone to Flesh} or by destroying the mural on which it is inscribed. If the mural is destroyed, all inscribed creatures on the destroyed portion of the mural are freed, restored to flesh, and are cured of this poison.</p>\n"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["arcane","incapacitation"],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"category":"offensive","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"loEXBExXiKbF4vnb","name":"Weightless Climber","type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":350000,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A hieroglyph scorpion can climb on any surface, even ceilings.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"category":"offensive","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"Fif9yDO3oKxqwlJ8","name":"Flatten","type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/OneAction.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":700000,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>The hieroglyph scorpion flattens itself against an adjacent wall, blending in seamlessly with the wall's paintings or inscriptions. While flattened, the scorpion has an automatic result of 35 on Deception checks and DCs to appear as just another part of the wall. If the hieroglyph scorpion attempts to do anything other than remain stationary or move along the wall's surface, it becomes unflattened and this effect ends.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["arcane","concentrate","polymorph"],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"action"},"category":"offensive","actions":{"value":1},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"ZR6LbvzCRNMlI9zS","name":"Attack of Opportunity","type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Reaction.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":800000,"flags":{"core":{}},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.AttackOfOpportunity]</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"attack-of-opportunity","_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"reaction"},"category":"defensive","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""},"weapon":{"value":""}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.hFtNbo1LKYCoDy2O","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"hXFfoRkSiyypYcHi","name":"Stinger","type":"melee","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/melee.svg","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"value":"","gm":""},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"value":["finesse","magical","reach-10"],"otherTags":[]},"damageRolls":{"4lqgmbw475h1d5p86z5c":{"damage":"2d8+13","damageType":"piercing","category":null}},"bonus":{"value":23},"attackEffects":{"value":["inscription-venom"]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"SjqTRBmKVnEvR29X","name":"Pincer","type":"melee","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/melee.svg","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Plus [[/r 1d6[bleed]]] damage</p>","gm":""},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"value":["agile","finesse","magical","reach-10"],"otherTags":[]},"damageRolls":{"tksimsrkawncaamtq2wq":{"damage":"2d6+13","damageType":"slashing","category":null}},"bonus":{"value":23},"attackEffects":{"value":[]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}}],"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{"pf2e":{"lootable":false},"core":{}},"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":110,"temp":0,"max":110,"details":"reanimation"},"ac":{"value":28,"details":"","base":28},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":40,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"climb","label":"Climb","value":40}],"details":"weightless climber"},"immunities":[{"type":"bleed"},{"type":"death-effects"},{"type":"disease"},{"type":"doomed"},{"type":"drained"},{"type":"fatigued"},{"type":"healing"},{"type":"mental"},{"type":"nonlethal-attacks"},{"type":"paralyzed"},{"type":"poison"},{"type":"sickened"},{"type":"unconscious"}],"weaknesses":[{"type":"precision","value":10}],"resistances":[{"type":"all-damage","value":10,"exceptions":["force","ghost-touch","precision"],"doubleVs":["non-magical"]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":[],"details":""},"level":{"value":10},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Hieroglyph scorpions are magical vermin originally constructed to guard pharaonic mausoleums, temples, and pyramids. Their unique ability to blend in with painted murals, chiseled inscriptions, and ornate sarcophagi allow them to tail tomb-robbers unseen, then leap out, attack, and disable would-be thieves.</p>\n<p>These incorporeal scorpions boast mighty defenses as their incomplete materialization allows them to flatten out and patrol two-dimensional surfaces. With long stingers and pincers, hieroglyph scorpions tend to keep their opponents at a distance, and are not above retreating from a lost fight.</p>\n<p>The hieroglyph scorpion's most fearsome weapon is its inscription venom, which gradually turns its victims to stone and adds them to the scorpion's ever-denser mural. But there is opportunity in danger. The halls protected by ancient hieroglyph scorpions are inscribed with countless unlucky treasure hunters. Destroying the mural could free them—and their loot.</p>\n<h2>Constructed Spirit</h2>\n<p>Though it lacks a physical body and has the incorporeal trait, a hieroglyph scorpion is not undead. Instead, it is a constructed being made from inanimate ethereal quintessence. Nevertheless, the powerful magic that creates a hieroglyph scorpion also binds it to the walls of the tomb it is ordered with protecting, enabling it to \"rejuvenate\" similarly to the way a ghost does.</p>\n<h2>Monster Part Subsystem</h2>\n<p><strong>Hieroglyph Scorpion Creature 10 </strong></p>\n<p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 125/275/500 gp</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (piercing, slashing), armor (medium), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Stealth)</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, charisma, dexterity, energy resistant (acid, cold, electricity, fire, negative, positive, sonic), poison, sensory (darkvision), wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary","authors":"Lau Bannenberg","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"creatureType":""},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":-5},"dex":{"mod":7},"con":{"mod":3},"int":{"mod":-5},"wis":{"mod":2},"cha":{"mod":6}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":20,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"},{"type":"tremorsense","acuity":"imprecise","range":120}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":15,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":21,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":18,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":21},"stealth":{"base":21,"special":[{"label":"While Flattened","base":25,"predicate":["flattened"]}]}},"traits":{"value":["construct","incorporeal","mindless"],"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"sm"}}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"prototypeToken":{"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"displayName":20,"displayBars":20,"flags":{"pf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":true}},"height":1,"width":1,"disposition":-1,"name":"Hieroglyph Scorpion","actorLink":false,"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"bar2":{"attribute":null},"randomImg":false,"light":{"alpha":0.25,"angle":360,"bright":0,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"speed":5,"intensity":5,"type":null,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1},"attenuation":0.5,"color":null,"negative":false,"priority